  "script": {
    "segments": [
      {
        "narration": "Twenty-six metres down off Japan sits a stone staircase. Yonaguni, the far western tip of the Ryukyu Islands. A diver found it in 1986.",
        "visual_query": "underwater rock terraces diver japan",
        "visual_fallback": "underwater rocks"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Flat terraces. Right angles. Walls that look cut. Kihachiro Aratake was out looking for hammerhead sharks when he swam into the thing.",
        "visual_query": "scuba diver reef okinawa japan",
        "visual_fallback": "scuba diver"
      },
      {
        "narration": "A Ryukyu University geologist, Masaaki Kimura, called it a sunken city. Pyramids, roads, a stadium. Was there a lost civilisation under Japan?",
        "visual_query": "ryukyu island coastline rocky cliffs",
        "visual_fallback": "island cliffs"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Other geologists dived it and found the answer in the rock itself. Sandstone, about twenty million years old, sliced through by parallel bedding planes and vertical fractures.",
        "visual_query": "layered sandstone cliff bedding planes",
        "visual_fallback": "layered sandstone"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Water prises those seams apart into steps and clean corners. And in forty years nobody has found a tool mark, a carving or a single artifact down there.",
        "visual_query": "ocean waves eroding rock shelf",
        "visual_fallback": "waves rocks"
      }
    ],
    "segment_count": 5,
    "word_count": 123,
    "duration_seconds": 35.0,
    "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
    "tts_rate": "+25%",
