        "claim": "The Yonaguni formation lies about 26 metres deep off Yonaguni Island in Japan's Ryukyu Islands and was noticed in 1986.",
        "segment_index": 0,
        "verdict": "SUPPORTED",
        "note": "Wikipedia: about 26 m (85 ft) deep below Arakawabana cliff, noticed in 1986.",
        "correction": null,
        "method": "claude-research",
        "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yonaguni_Monument"
      },
      {
        "claim": "Kihachiro Aratake, a local tourism association director, spotted the formation while looking for hammerhead sharks.",
        "segment_index": 1,
        "verdict": "SUPPORTED",
        "note": "75% of the claim's wording appears in the reference article",
        "correction": null,
        "method": "wikipedia-lexical"
      },
      {
        "claim": "Masaaki Kimura of the University of the Ryukyus argued the formation is man-made, identifying a pyramid, roads and a stadium.",
        "segment_index": 2,
        "verdict": "SUPPORTED",
        "note": "82% of the claim's wording appears in the reference article",
        "correction": null,
        "method": "wikipedia-lexical"
      },
      {
        "claim": "The formation is Early Miocene sandstone and mudstone roughly 20 million years old, cut by parallel bedding planes and vertical joints.",
        "segment_index": 3,
        "verdict": "SUPPORTED",
        "note": "87% of the claim's wording appears in the reference article, including 1 number(s)",
        "correction": null,
        "method": "wikipedia-lexical"
      },
      {
        "claim": "Geologists including Robert Schoch attribute the steps and right angles to erosion along those seams, and no artifacts or tool marks have been found at the site.",
        "segment_index": 4,
        "verdict": "SUPPORTED",
        "note": "Schoch, Wichmann and Ogata et al. (2019) all attribute the features to weathering and erosion; no artifacts are reported, and a 2024 Kyushu University survey found no traces of human activity. The narration's 'forty years' counts from the 1986 discovery.",
        "correction": null,
        "method": "claude-research",
